WEBVTT

00:05.680 --> 00:10.960
This section is called mixed numbers, but you'll see a lot of lessons in this section about both mixed

00:10.960 --> 00:13.570
numbers and improper fractions.

00:13.780 --> 00:14.590
Why?

00:14.620 --> 00:19.390
Well, because mixed numbers and improper fractions are just two different ways of expressing the same

00:19.390 --> 00:19.990
thing.

00:20.020 --> 00:22.840
That's why it makes so much sense for us to learn them together.

00:23.380 --> 00:30.340
So if you have one and a half apples, you could express that with fractions as the mixed number one

00:30.340 --> 00:34.810
and one half apples or as the improper fraction.

00:34.930 --> 00:37.870
Three halves apples or three over two apples.

00:38.200 --> 00:41.410
Both of these express exactly the same value.

00:41.530 --> 00:42.970
One and a half apples.

00:43.000 --> 00:46.030
They're just written in two different ways.

00:46.480 --> 00:51.040
We'll start this section by introducing mixed numbers, improper fractions in the relationship between

00:51.040 --> 00:56.200
them, and then we'll move into the rules we'll use for arithmetic with these kinds of numbers.
